[[Image:Гермашев_Со-звездой_1916.jpg|thumb|Коледуване]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|bg|sla-pro|*kolęda}}, from {{der|bg|la|kalendae||first day of the month}}. Originally referring to a [[pagan]] winter festival, where [[caroller]]s (typically men or children) visit households and wish the hosts abundant and healthy incoming year.

===Pronunciation===
* {{bg-IPA|Ко́леда}}

===Proper noun===
{{bg-proper noun|Ко́леда|f|adj=ко́леден}}

# {{lb|bg|obsolete}} [[carolling]]
#: {{syn|bg|коледу́ване|кола́дство|q2=dialectal}}
# [[Christmas]]
#: {{syn|bg|Рождество Христово|Божич}}
#: {{uxi|bg|на Коледа|at Christmas}}
#: {{uxi|bg|по Коледа|at Christmastide}}
#: {{uxi|bg|[[сух|су́ха]]/[[малък|ма́лка]] '''Ко́леда'''|the day before Christmas}}
#: {{uxi|bg|[[Честита Коледа]]|[[Merry Christmas]]}}
#: {{uxi|bg|[[Дядо Коледа]]|Father Christmas, [[Santa Claus]]}}

